From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anna Sato <annasato@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 06:39:46 -0700
Subject: Fix Browser-process Heap-UAF in LockManager caused by stale
 SharedWorkerHost

SharedWorkerHost unconditionally registers as a Web Locks observer in
CreateLockManager(), but only removed itself in ~SharedWorkerHost()
inside an if (site_instance_->HasProcess()) block. When the worker host
is destroyed after its renderer process has exited, deregistration was
skipped, leaving a dangling pointer in LockManager::client_observer_map_
that triggered a heap-use-after-free during subsequent lock contention.

This CL fixes the issue by updating SharedWorkerHost::GetStoragePartitionImpl()
to return service_->storage_partition(), which is valid throughout the
entire lifetime of SharedWorkerHost, and unconditionally removing the
lock observer in ~SharedWorkerHost(). In addition, client_observer_map_
in LockManager is hardened to use raw_ptr<Observer>.

